{"severity":"warning","file":"errors/parallel_shared_write_1.march","start_line":8,"start_col":41,"end_line":8,"end_col":70,"message":"Every parallel call writes the same Vault key `\"max\"`.","code":"parallel_shared_write","fix":null,"labels":[],"notes":["`List.pmap` runs this function on many elements at once, and every call writes the same key `\"max\"`. The calls finish in no fixed order, so which value is left is a race, and a read-then-write of the key loses updates.","Return the values from the function and combine the results after the parallel call, or key each write by the element. For a shared counter use `Vault.incr`, which adds under one lock."],"category":"CONCURRENCY"}
